# Front-end assets pinned by content, not just by version.
#
# One source of truth for two jobs:
#   1. the `integrity="sha384-…"` attributes in web/index.html (browser-side), and
#   2. `make vendor`, which refuses to write a file whose digest doesn't match.
#
# Every path is <package>@<version>/<path-inside-the-npm-tarball> — the same shape
# jsDelivr and unpkg serve, so ASSET_BASE can flip between CDN and /vendor without
# touching a URL. Digests are of the published npm bytes.
#
# To upgrade a dependency: change the version here and in web/index.html, run
# `make vendor` to fetch it, then copy the digest it reports into both files.

